{"number":2129,"title":"Author cloudflare-site/internal-links-omit-html-extension as a check","body":"Landed as prose for now (`packs/cloudflare-site/RULES.md`): Workers static assets 307s a `.html`
path request to its extensionless form, so an internal link that still names the `.html` file
costs every visitor that redirect.

MissingBulbWebsite had already written this as a local-pack check
(`internal-links-omit-html-extension`, scanning `site/**/*.html` for `href="...X.html"`). A
canon version, generalized off the wrangler config's `assets.directory` rather than a hardcoded
`site/`, was drafted and tested in this session — it worked, but authoring it as a NEW blocking
`worldRule` trips `consumer-safe-change` (a rule that just became blocking needs either a
migration record or a rehearsal fixture), and the honest discharge for a purely additive check is
the fixture — `vendoring/rehearsal/fixtures.mjs`, outside `packs/`. The growth-promote task that
would otherwise land this is scoped to write only under the corpus roots (`promote-scope`,
blocking on the promote branch), so it cannot touch that file; a migration record would be the
wrong tool here (nothing needs migrating for an additive check), so per `task.md`'s own fallback
this lands as prose plus this issue instead of a silently-shipped broken check.

The drafted rule + test (deleted from the promote branch,
`missingbulb/Claudinite#2032` / `missingbulb/Claudinite#2117`, so a session working this issue
can restore them rather than re-derive):

```js
// packs/cloudflare-site/worldRules/internal-links-omit-html-extension.mjs
import { finding } from '../../../engine/checks/helpers/findings.mjs';
import { parseWranglerConfig, publishedDir, wranglerConfigPath } from '../lib.mjs';

const INTERNAL_HTML_HREF = /href=["'](?!https?:\/\/|mailto:)([^"']*\.html)["']/gi;

const rule = {
  id: 'cloudflare-site/internal-links-omit-html-extension',
  severity: 'blocking',
  since: '2026-09-18',
  description: 'An internal link inside the published tree names the extensionless path, never the .html file',
  doc: 'packs/cloudflare-site/RULES.md',
  why: 'Workers static assets 307s the .html form to the extensionless path, so a .html internal link costs every visitor that redirect',

  run(ctx) {
    const configPath = wranglerConfigPath(ctx.tracked);
    const dir = configPath && publishedDir(parseWranglerConfig(ctx.read(configPath)), configPath);
    if (!dir) return [];

    const out = [];
    for (const file of ctx.tracked.filter((f) => f.startsWith(`${dir}/`) && f.endsWith('.html'))) {
      const raw = ctx.read(file);
      if (raw === null) continue;
      raw.split('\n').forEach((line, i) => {
        for (const [, href] of line.matchAll(INTERNAL_HTML_HREF)) {
          out.push(finding(rule, {
            file,
            line: i + 1,
            what: `internal link still points at the .html file: ${href}`,
            fix: 'drop the .html suffix and link to the extensionless path — the .html form still resolves through the redirect, so nothing breaks meanwhile',
          }));
        }
      });
    }
    return out;
  },
};

export default rule;
```

Its `ruleTester` fixture test (`packs/cloudflare-site/test/worldRules/internal-links-omit-html-extension.test.mjs`)
passed clean/flagged cases covering: no wrangler config, an already-extensionless link, an
external `.html` link, a `mailto:` link, a `.html` file outside the published tree, a relative
internal `.html` link, and a bare-filename `.html` link (with its line number).

To close this: land the rule + test, add its row to `packs/cloudflare-site/README.md`'s Checks
table, and add the fixture in `vendoring/rehearsal/fixtures.mjs` that discharges
`consumer-safe-change` — the existing `cloudflare-site-consumer` fixture's `site/index.html`
already carries no internal `.html` link, so it should need only a comment update (four checks →
five) once this session's draft is restored, plus a rerun of
`node --test vendoring/rehearsal/rehearsal.test.mjs` to confirm both its fresh and stale
rehearsals stay green.

